WEBVTT

00:15.439 --> 00:17.065
Say, Minato…

00:21.403 --> 00:23.822
What do you think of Koyun?

00:30.996 --> 00:32.372
I'd see her around.

00:33.248 --> 00:36.793
I figured she was different
from the other girls at school.

00:38.045 --> 00:39.337
So I remembered her face.

00:40.714 --> 00:41.840
Then…

00:46.762 --> 00:48.138
<i>She's by herself again.</i>

00:49.014 --> 00:52.017
<i>I kept following her with my eyes</i>
<i>every time we crossed paths.</i>

00:52.517 --> 00:54.019
<i>I always thought…</i>

00:55.270 --> 00:58.190
I guess I felt pity for her.

01:00.275 --> 01:01.276
Minato.

01:02.360 --> 01:05.322
You're always like this.
Aren't you, Minato?

01:05.405 --> 01:08.158
You're always pitying people.
"Poor you," or "She's alone."

01:08.658 --> 01:11.703
That is so sanctimonious of you.

01:12.287 --> 01:13.330
Sanctimonious?

01:14.539 --> 01:15.749
It is.

01:16.875 --> 01:19.544
<i>Slapping a "poor you" sticker on someone…</i>

01:20.128 --> 01:23.799
<i>Do you have any idea how empty inside</i>
<i>that can make someone feel?</i>

01:24.549 --> 01:27.969
You only do it so people look to you.

01:28.053 --> 01:29.888
You want them to depend on you.

01:30.889 --> 01:33.683
Do not try to wile your way in
with Koyun like that.

03:07.569 --> 03:11.990
EPISODE 4
IMPENETRABLE

03:12.991 --> 03:16.578
What gives you the right to decide
whether someone should be "pitied"?

03:17.579 --> 03:21.207
You shouldn't force Koyun
into some narrow mold you just made up.

03:22.834 --> 03:24.377
You may be right.

03:25.712 --> 03:27.213
But that was only at the start.

03:27.714 --> 03:29.132
Hikawa,

03:29.215 --> 03:32.385
I always thought,
"She is so pitiful." But…

03:33.428 --> 03:35.472
<i>it was all just a misconception.</i>

03:36.473 --> 03:37.474
<i>Now…</i>

03:39.309 --> 03:41.603
I'm in this for a different reason.

03:41.686 --> 03:42.729
So don't you worry.

03:44.022 --> 03:47.067
I don't think
you're quite her type, Minato.

03:47.150 --> 03:48.193
That's not what I meant.

03:48.276 --> 03:51.196
And even if it were,
you could at least sugarcoat it a bit.

03:51.696 --> 03:55.951
Well, whatever! Just don't go
getting close to Koyun for weird reasons.

03:56.034 --> 03:58.870
Surely we're allowed to
talk to each other?

03:59.454 --> 04:01.498
Why, are you her guardian?

04:02.540 --> 04:04.626
Spare the rod,
and you spoil the child, sweetie.

04:06.336 --> 04:10.632
I just don't want to hurt Koyun anymore.

04:11.341 --> 04:13.885
<i>Not "I don't want her getting hurt"?</i>

04:15.762 --> 04:18.139
But wait, the name "Hikawa"…

04:18.723 --> 04:19.975
Was she in the basketball club?

04:20.058 --> 04:20.892
EEK

04:21.476 --> 04:22.727
I knew it.

04:22.811 --> 04:25.063
Now I get why you were so angry.

04:25.146 --> 04:26.147
FLUSTERED, FLUSTERED

04:30.151 --> 04:35.073
This is exactly why I didn't want you and
Koyun getting involved with each other!

04:35.156 --> 04:38.159
Why can Yota get involved but not me, huh?

04:38.243 --> 04:40.787
Because you pick up on things!

04:40.870 --> 04:43.081
And what, Yota is oblivious?

04:43.164 --> 04:44.249
No, it's not that…

04:44.332 --> 04:45.583
That's a little uncalled for.

04:45.667 --> 04:46.668
I didn't mean that…

04:50.588 --> 04:51.673
Wow.

04:51.756 --> 04:53.300
They're so different.

04:53.383 --> 04:55.302
Yours is like a sumo wrestler's.

04:55.385 --> 04:57.304
What kind of comparison is that?

04:57.387 --> 04:58.430
Must be nice…

04:58.513 --> 04:59.681
Nice?

05:00.265 --> 05:04.144
I always wanted to palm the ball like this
when I was in the basketball club.

05:04.644 --> 05:06.688
But I just couldn't do it.

05:06.771 --> 05:08.815
Well, with those hands…

05:11.276 --> 05:13.403
Wait, huh? Basketball club?

05:13.486 --> 05:16.740
You were in the basketball club?
Why didn't you say so?

05:17.741 --> 05:20.368
I never played the way you do.

05:21.077 --> 05:22.996
I actually quit halfway.

05:33.590 --> 05:36.468
You mentioned feeling empty inside
at being pitied by others.

05:37.844 --> 05:42.766
Is that how you've felt
ever since I reached out to you?

05:42.849 --> 05:44.142
EEK

05:44.225 --> 05:45.226
FLUSTERED, FLUSTERED

05:45.310 --> 05:46.895
That…

05:48.646 --> 05:49.981
I'm sorry.

05:50.065 --> 05:51.900
You're right. I probably was pitying you.

05:54.110 --> 05:55.987
TOP GRADES GUARANTEED
CRAM SCHOOL

06:00.116 --> 06:03.578
<i>I reached out to you because I thought</i>
<i>you looked bored there on your own.</i>

06:04.579 --> 06:07.207
But now that we're friends,

06:07.290 --> 06:09.959
I don't see you in that way anymore.

06:10.585 --> 06:16.257
We became friends, Yota joined the group,
and we've had so much fun together

06:17.175 --> 06:20.178
that I was unable to see
that you were feeling this way.

06:21.513 --> 06:23.431
I'm sorry for hurting you.

06:26.476 --> 06:27.894
Minato…

06:31.064 --> 06:33.399
Why are you like this?
Personal distance, dude!

06:33.983 --> 06:36.486
I've enjoyed
our time together too, you know?

06:36.569 --> 06:38.613
And you've saved my butt heaps.

06:38.696 --> 06:40.156
Geez!

06:40.740 --> 06:43.159
So we gotta keep being friends, okay?

06:47.997 --> 06:49.207
Yep. Friends.

06:49.916 --> 06:51.292
You'll dirty your sweater…

06:51.376 --> 06:53.545
Don't worry. It's not clean to begin with.

06:53.628 --> 06:55.213
RUB RUB

06:55.296 --> 06:56.297
Excuse me?

06:58.299 --> 07:00.301
<i>Now I get it.</i>

07:01.219 --> 07:03.680
<i>Maybe all I ever wanted</i>

07:03.763 --> 07:07.934
<i>was just to be friends with him</i>
<i>on equal footing.</i>

07:11.271 --> 07:13.064
<i>Man, I'm such a child!</i>

07:15.233 --> 07:16.317
Miki?

07:17.193 --> 07:19.654
Geez! Wait up!

07:20.488 --> 07:22.949
They did go to get drinks, right?

07:23.032 --> 07:24.033
SLUMP

07:24.117 --> 07:25.618
They sure are taking their time.

07:25.702 --> 07:28.121
Do you think maybe they're out
growing their own cocoa beans?

07:28.204 --> 07:29.205
COCOA

07:29.289 --> 07:30.540
From scratch?

07:32.292 --> 07:34.711
Sorry to keep you waiting.

07:34.794 --> 07:36.254
DOUBLE EXTRA RED BEAN SOUP RICH

07:36.337 --> 07:39.674
Check it out. New products!
"Double Extra Red Bean Soup Rich!"

07:39.757 --> 07:40.842
We can share!

07:41.426 --> 07:42.844
Apparently, it's mandatory.

07:49.184 --> 07:51.853
Sounds like a ramen menu item!
This'll definitely clear my head.

07:51.936 --> 07:53.021
Right?

07:53.104 --> 07:55.940
This is just the pick-me-up we need
to get us through those exams.

07:56.024 --> 07:58.735
<i>Did something happen with Miki?</i>

08:02.572 --> 08:04.991
<i>Should I even be asking her this?</i>

08:07.076 --> 08:08.244
Miki…

08:09.329 --> 08:13.750
Did something happen between you
and Amamiya when you went to buy drinks?

08:15.668 --> 08:17.003
Well…

08:17.086 --> 08:18.630
<i>A lot happened.</i>

08:19.547 --> 08:22.675
We talked about that time
you bought that curry drink.

08:22.759 --> 08:23.885
Why?

08:24.469 --> 08:28.306
He said he made you buy it on accident,
so he was paying you back for it today.

08:28.389 --> 08:29.390
HE NEVER SAID ANYTHING

08:29.474 --> 08:31.142
What? He didn't have to worry about that.

08:31.226 --> 08:34.729
You see? He never said anything
because he knew you'd feel bad.

08:34.812 --> 08:35.855
- <i>Bye-bye.</i>
- <i>See you.</i>

08:35.939 --> 08:38.149
No! Feels like I'm losing
what we learned today!

08:38.233 --> 08:40.401
Wait… Notebook… I must review…

08:40.485 --> 08:43.071
No, wait! Don't leave my brain!

08:43.905 --> 08:48.076
<i>Still, none of what she said just now</i>
<i>should have been enough to make her cry?</i>

08:51.871 --> 08:53.998
<i>The time for cramming for exams is over.</i>

08:54.082 --> 08:55.166
SECOND SEMESTER FINAL EXAMS

08:55.250 --> 08:57.168
FIRST PERIOD: ENGLISH COMMUNICATION I
SECOND PERIOD: PUBLIC STUDIES

08:57.252 --> 08:58.795
<i>It's the first day of exams.</i>

09:01.422 --> 09:02.423
Begin.

09:08.596 --> 09:10.431
<i>It really is exactly the same.</i>

09:10.515 --> 09:11.683
<i>Thank you, past exams.</i>

09:13.685 --> 09:16.437
<i>This is what we went through</i>
<i>during Yota's seminar!</i>

09:16.521 --> 09:18.189
FIRST PERIOD:
ENGLISH COMMUNICATION I

09:18.273 --> 09:19.899
SECOND PERIOD: PUBLIC STUDIES

09:19.983 --> 09:21.943
THIRD PERIOD:
FUNDAMENTALS OF CHEMISTRY

09:24.279 --> 09:26.698
<i>Off to a good start! Yay!</i>

09:29.033 --> 09:30.952
SECOND SEMESTER
FINAL EXAMS - DAY TWO

09:31.035 --> 09:33.955
<i>I've got it! I've got it this time!</i>

09:43.256 --> 09:44.674
All right. Time's up.

10:05.028 --> 10:06.112
<i>Messages.</i>

10:06.195 --> 10:07.196
NINE
UNREAD: 9

10:07.280 --> 10:08.489
<i>Wow, so many…</i>

10:09.115 --> 10:12.577
<i>Koyun! Let's grab lunch</i>
<i>before heading home.</i>

10:12.660 --> 10:14.787
<i>Oops, this is the group chat.</i>
<i>Wanna come, Yota?</i>

10:14.871 --> 10:16.497
<i>Oops, that wasn't an afterthought.</i>

10:16.581 --> 10:18.041
<i>Please join us. Whimper…</i>

10:18.124 --> 10:19.125
LOL

10:19.208 --> 10:21.210
- <i>I'll come.</i>
- <i>Koyun! Come on!</i>

10:22.211 --> 10:24.213
Found you, Koyun!

10:26.716 --> 10:29.761
Looks like we're first to meet up.

10:30.345 --> 10:32.305
Do you think Miki
is still in the classroom?

10:37.018 --> 10:38.061
What's up, Miki?

10:38.144 --> 10:40.355
Hey, Minato. Where's Yota?

10:40.438 --> 10:41.606
He's already downstairs.

10:41.689 --> 10:44.025
Really?

10:44.108 --> 10:46.235
- Did you need him for something?
- Not exactly…

10:46.319 --> 10:49.405
Me and Koyun were just about
to go out for lunch with him.

10:51.240 --> 10:53.910
- What's this, Miki?
- You're freezing!

10:53.993 --> 10:56.954
Were you trying to leave me out of things?

10:57.038 --> 10:58.665
No! Not at all!

11:01.250 --> 11:03.169
Stare…

11:03.920 --> 11:07.006
Yeah, I'm totally stumped.
Are there really five more differences?

11:07.090 --> 11:09.175
- Number of grapes?
- Already checked.

11:09.258 --> 11:10.677
Found one.

11:10.760 --> 11:11.803
And here's another.

11:12.845 --> 11:14.931
Hey, wait! Minato, you're too quick.

11:15.014 --> 11:17.809
We gotta find them all,
or else our doria won't come.

11:17.892 --> 11:19.185
Is that how it works?

11:21.312 --> 11:24.482
<i>They seem to be on good terms.</i>

11:25.066 --> 11:26.442
<i>That's good.</i>

11:27.318 --> 11:28.945
<i>Maybe I'm just overthinking things.</i>

11:29.028 --> 11:31.948
SPACING OUT

11:32.031 --> 11:34.075
Have you been here before, Hikawa?

11:35.535 --> 11:37.537
Oh, no. This is my first time.

11:38.371 --> 11:40.790
I usually just go straight home
from school.

11:45.378 --> 11:47.713
<i>Watch it with those pitiful eyes there!</i>

11:47.797 --> 11:49.215
WELL?

11:49.799 --> 11:50.925
<i>That's not it.</i>

11:52.176 --> 11:54.345
- Thank you for the meal.
- Thank you for the meal.

11:54.929 --> 11:57.056
<i>That was pretty tasty for being so cheap.</i>

12:00.893 --> 12:03.896
You're not in any clubs, are you, Hikawa?

12:04.439 --> 12:05.690
Do you work part-time?

12:07.316 --> 12:10.236
Yeah. But I don't get many shifts.

12:10.319 --> 12:11.612
Where do you work?

12:11.696 --> 12:12.697
REGULAR CUSTOMERS

12:12.780 --> 12:13.990
Just a local restaurant.

12:14.073 --> 12:17.118
Only the local elderly come to visit.
It's very laid-back.

12:17.201 --> 12:19.370
What do you do on your days off?

12:19.454 --> 12:21.581
Come on, Minato…

12:22.915 --> 12:24.500
What do I do?

12:25.543 --> 12:27.003
<i>I read…</i>

12:30.256 --> 12:31.966
What's this? Looks lame.

12:32.925 --> 12:34.177
<i>I watch movies…</i>

12:34.677 --> 12:36.471
You like this stuff?

12:36.971 --> 12:38.848
<i>I study ahead…</i>

12:38.931 --> 12:40.099
<i>You're such a nerd!</i>

12:42.226 --> 12:43.686
I don't really do anything.

12:44.812 --> 12:47.190
I kind of just do a lot of nothing.

12:47.690 --> 12:50.860
Oh, really? That's a pity.

12:50.943 --> 12:51.944
GLARE

12:52.028 --> 12:55.156
Koyun gets super busy hanging out with me!

12:55.239 --> 12:56.491
Is that so?

13:01.787 --> 13:04.123
- Are you paying separately?
- Yes, please.

13:04.707 --> 13:06.834
Hey, Minato. What were you thinking?

13:06.918 --> 13:09.879
Why you gotta be so pushy?
I did tell you, didn't I?

13:09.962 --> 13:12.089
Yes, but…

13:12.173 --> 13:14.759
<i>How boring must it be</i>
<i>if we're the only ones chatting?</i>

13:14.842 --> 13:15.843
RUB RUB

13:17.094 --> 13:18.846
- You're right!
- You see?

13:22.850 --> 13:26.354
<i>I get a little tired of all the questions.</i>

13:28.940 --> 13:30.399
I am so full!

13:30.483 --> 13:34.320
<i>I'm with different people, and the context</i>
<i>is completely different now,</i>

13:34.946 --> 13:37.865
<i>but I'm still not very good</i>
<i>at talking about myself.</i>

13:39.367 --> 13:40.868
<i>It's not that I hate doing it.</i>

13:41.536 --> 13:44.497
<i>I'm just scared of people</i>
<i>seeing the real me.</i>

13:45.206 --> 13:47.333
<i>I don't want to be rejected.</i>

13:47.833 --> 13:50.962
<i>I don't want to hate myself</i>
<i>more than I already do now.</i>

13:52.338 --> 13:55.383
<i>So when people reach out,</i>
<i>I keep my distance.</i>

13:56.092 --> 13:57.927
You're weird.

14:00.137 --> 14:01.764
<i>What even is "normal"?</i>

14:05.476 --> 14:07.645
FINISH! SECOND SEMESTER
FINAL EXAMS DAY 3

14:07.728 --> 14:10.648
- Good job on the exams!
- Yay!

14:10.731 --> 14:12.650
EXAM AFTER-PARTY
IN GRADE 1 CLASS 5

14:12.733 --> 14:14.860
Want one? It's strawberry flavor.

14:14.944 --> 14:16.070
Thank you!

14:17.738 --> 14:20.950
Once again, Azumi is positively radiant.

14:23.494 --> 14:24.912
THUNK

14:24.996 --> 14:26.747
<i>I feel awful…</i>

14:27.248 --> 14:30.334
<i>I managed to push through the exams,</i>

14:30.418 --> 14:33.170
<i>but my stomach is doing somersaults.</i>

14:33.254 --> 14:35.172
NURSE'S OFFICE

14:35.756 --> 14:37.300
Noriko…

14:38.885 --> 14:41.304
You're just here to chill out again.

14:41.387 --> 14:43.890
This is not your private
little get-warm place.

14:43.973 --> 14:46.475
No… I'm actually sick today…

14:46.976 --> 14:48.311
Oh, my.

14:53.482 --> 14:54.650
My stomach hurts.

14:55.651 --> 14:57.111
Oh, dear. Is it stress?

14:57.194 --> 14:59.238
Or did you eat something off?

14:59.322 --> 15:01.782
I haven't eaten anything today.

15:02.408 --> 15:04.368
I did have three coffees though.

15:04.911 --> 15:06.454
That'll do it.

15:06.537 --> 15:08.706
Stay here and sleep until you feel better.

15:09.290 --> 15:11.792
I don't like the feeling of being in bed
in my school uniform.

15:11.876 --> 15:13.711
Well, beggars can't be choosers.

15:19.091 --> 15:21.260
Hey, got any of your old
middle school classmates here?

15:21.344 --> 15:23.846
Oh, yeah. A super nerd, that one.

15:23.930 --> 15:24.931
MEITEN HIGH SCHOOL

15:25.014 --> 15:27.183
Well, you gotta be smart
to get into Meiten.

15:28.434 --> 15:30.603
How about you, Igarashi?
Any old middle school classmates?

15:33.189 --> 15:34.565
Don't know.

15:34.649 --> 15:36.943
I doubt it. Who'd come here…

15:37.944 --> 15:40.696
We've got so many leftover snacks.

15:40.780 --> 15:42.073
Think we bought too many?

15:42.156 --> 15:43.449
Definitely.

15:43.532 --> 15:44.992
Hey, look. Students from West High.

15:48.204 --> 15:49.330
Igarashi?

15:52.875 --> 15:54.085
- What?
- What?

15:58.839 --> 16:00.132
What?

16:00.216 --> 16:01.425
Sorry, guys!

16:01.509 --> 16:04.345
You go on ahead.
I found an old friend from middle school.

16:04.428 --> 16:05.471
All right.

16:05.972 --> 16:06.973
Bye-bye!

16:07.723 --> 16:09.225
What are you doing here?

16:11.644 --> 16:14.438
Azumi. You…

16:16.691 --> 16:19.402
You've, like, completely changed.

16:19.485 --> 16:20.695
What happened to the gorilla?

16:22.029 --> 16:23.531
Shut up, you!

16:26.325 --> 16:27.410
Come here.

16:28.619 --> 16:30.663
Why are you here?

16:31.372 --> 16:33.290
For club. Club activities.

16:33.374 --> 16:35.710
Joint practice, you know?

16:37.378 --> 16:40.089
And hey,
I didn't know you got into Meiten.

16:40.589 --> 16:43.884
I'll bet you're the only one
who commutes this far every day.

16:44.385 --> 16:45.678
Why bother?

16:46.262 --> 16:49.306
<i>Does he not know Koyun goes here too?</i>

16:51.392 --> 16:54.311
Hey, Igarashi! What are you doing?

16:56.772 --> 16:58.691
- Sorry.
- See ya.

17:02.153 --> 17:04.572
Who was that? She's super cute.

17:04.655 --> 17:06.323
Are you blind or something?

17:06.407 --> 17:07.408
What?

17:08.117 --> 17:11.704
<i>Koyun…</i>
<i>Please, please have gone home already…</i>

17:17.043 --> 17:18.169
<i>It's so dark!</i>

17:19.045 --> 17:20.046
<i>What time is it?</i>

17:21.547 --> 17:23.299
<i>Is it because the curtains are pulled?</i>

17:23.799 --> 17:25.217
<i>Thank you, Noriko.</i>

17:25.801 --> 17:29.930
<i>It's still light out,</i>
<i>so I can't have been out that long…</i>

17:35.561 --> 17:36.812
<i>Igarashi!</i>

17:38.147 --> 17:39.482
<i>That's right. It was today.</i>

17:40.066 --> 17:43.652
Well, he's coming to our school, but
you wouldn't recognize each other then.

17:43.736 --> 17:44.779
When is that?

17:44.862 --> 17:47.656
During club activities on the afternoon
of the last day of exams.

17:48.574 --> 17:50.076
<i>I knew this…</i>

17:51.243 --> 17:52.411
Hey, by the way…

17:52.495 --> 17:54.997
I ran into Azumi earlier.

17:55.081 --> 17:57.416
Do you know her? Is she in your class?

17:57.500 --> 18:00.377
Miki? We're in different classes,
but we're good friends.

18:01.003 --> 18:04.590
Does she cause trouble here too?
No broken windows anywhere?

18:05.841 --> 18:07.176
She's fine.

18:07.802 --> 18:09.804
I ran into Azumi earlier.

18:10.554 --> 18:12.431
<i>They're talking about Miki.</i>

18:13.015 --> 18:14.016
<i>Why?</i>

18:15.309 --> 18:17.186
<i>It's no good. I can't hear them.</i>

18:19.021 --> 18:21.190
Hikawa? What are you doing?

18:24.318 --> 18:26.070
You feeling better now?

18:26.153 --> 18:27.363
I am.

18:27.446 --> 18:28.656
Ready to go home?

18:28.739 --> 18:29.949
Yes.

18:32.535 --> 18:34.912
<i>I need to leave quickly</i>
<i>so he doesn't notice me.</i>

18:38.290 --> 18:41.877
<i>I couldn't quite catch it,</i>
<i>but they were talking about Miki.</i>

18:41.961 --> 18:44.255
<i>They wouldn't go on</i>
<i>to talk about me, would they?</i>

18:47.633 --> 18:51.804
<i>Amamiya wouldn't bring up my name…</i>
<i>Would he?</i>

18:52.805 --> 18:54.515
Do you know a guy named Igarashi?

18:54.598 --> 18:55.808
Where do you work?

18:55.891 --> 18:57.601
What do you do on your days off?

18:57.685 --> 18:58.686
OBSESSED WITH OTHERS

18:58.769 --> 19:00.229
<i>I think he will.</i>

19:02.314 --> 19:03.482
<i>I don't like this.</i>

19:04.733 --> 19:07.153
<i>I don't want people</i>
<i>to be interested in me.</i>

19:12.825 --> 19:16.245
<i>I don't want people knowing the real me.</i>

19:18.914 --> 19:20.374
Hey. Igarashi?

19:20.457 --> 19:22.626
Do you remember Hikawa?

19:29.466 --> 19:30.843
Morning.

19:36.891 --> 19:38.017
Hey, Hikawa.

19:39.476 --> 19:40.561
Morning!

19:40.644 --> 19:41.645
WARM AND TOASTY

19:42.897 --> 19:45.149
<i>He seems warm and toasty for some reason.</i>

19:45.774 --> 19:48.152
Amamiya… Did you run here?

19:48.819 --> 19:50.863
We just finished morning practice.

19:50.946 --> 19:52.656
I must be steaming in the cold.

19:52.740 --> 19:54.575
<i>Morning practice…</i>

19:54.658 --> 19:56.410
<i>I remember those days…</i>

19:57.953 --> 20:00.039
By the way, Igarashi was here yesterday.

20:02.541 --> 20:05.794
But you're not interested in him, are you?

20:06.587 --> 20:08.714
I mean, you weren't all that close
with him, were you?

20:11.926 --> 20:13.385
<i>Why is he being like this?</i>

20:13.886 --> 20:17.389
Was Igarashi quite the prominent
figure in middle school?

20:18.265 --> 20:20.809
Yeah… I guess you could say that…

20:21.477 --> 20:24.104
<i>He was always the center of attention.</i>

20:24.188 --> 20:26.315
<i>He was constantly surrounded by people.</i>

20:26.899 --> 20:29.443
Yeah? I had a hunch he might have been.

20:30.027 --> 20:35.532
<i>He's the kind of person who barges</i>
<i>into your heart without any consideration.</i>

20:37.201 --> 20:38.202
I'm sorry.

20:38.786 --> 20:40.704
Maybe we should give middle school a rest.

20:44.291 --> 20:48.212
There's plenty of new memories
to make right here in high school.

20:48.295 --> 20:51.507
So many new events,
so we should look forward to those, right?

20:53.801 --> 20:57.721
<i>I've never spoken to Amamiya</i>
<i>about my time in middle school.</i>

20:58.555 --> 21:00.557
<i>So why bring it up now?</i>

21:02.893 --> 21:05.771
<i>Did Igarashi say something to him?</i>

21:06.814 --> 21:08.983
<i>What did he say?</i>

21:09.566 --> 21:13.112
Hey, are you and Igarashi going out?

21:13.195 --> 21:15.906
Yo, what base are you at?

21:16.699 --> 21:17.908
GIRLS BASKETBALL CLUB

21:17.992 --> 21:20.119
She is such a Pick Me, isn't she?

21:20.202 --> 21:21.328
I can't stand her.

21:22.496 --> 21:23.998
- Did you hear?
- About Igarashi…

21:24.081 --> 21:26.166
- At her house…
- No way, really?

21:26.250 --> 21:28.877
- So it's all true?
- No way!

21:29.461 --> 21:32.047
<i>Why must people love to gossip so much?</i>

21:32.756 --> 21:34.717
<i>Why can't they just leave me alone?</i>

21:34.800 --> 21:36.260
<i>Hey, Koyuki.</i>

21:37.678 --> 21:40.222
<i>Is it really that fun to mess with people?</i>

21:40.806 --> 21:42.933
<i>Just tell us the truth already.</i>

21:43.600 --> 21:45.394
<i>You don't care about the truth.</i>

21:45.477 --> 21:47.896
<i>You only care that it's entertaining.</i>

21:52.985 --> 21:54.236
<i>No more…</i>

21:56.739 --> 21:58.490
<i>No more letting people in…</i>

21:59.783 --> 22:00.784
Why?

22:02.119 --> 22:03.620
WARM AND TOASTY

22:03.704 --> 22:05.372
That cool air feels nice.

22:07.041 --> 22:08.042
Koyun--

22:08.125 --> 22:10.502
Why must you stick your nose
into other people's business?

22:14.965 --> 22:16.550
I don't get it…

22:19.845 --> 22:21.013
You disgust me.

23:50.352 --> 23:55.357
Subtitle translation by: Rychelle Brittain
